failure_modes.scientific_principle:
EKF linearizes the nonlinear functions using first-order Taylor expansion:
  f(x) ≈ f(μ) + F_x·(x − μ)  where F_x = ∂f/∂x |_{x=μ}
  h(x) ≈ h(μ) + H_x·(x − μ)  where H_x = ∂h/∂x |_{x=μ}
The Jacobians F_x and H_x replace A and H in the standard KF equations. Key insight: linearization error grows with nonlinearity of f/h and with uncertainty σ. EKF is accurate when the uncertainty is small (tracking mode) but fails for large uncertainties (global localization mode).
